MEASUREMENT EVIDENCE for br-r37-c1-degframe (the commit message carries none).

This change was authored and validated in a session that had not yet committed
it; it was picked up from the shared working tree and committed verbatim. The
numbers below are the ones it was validated against.

Profiled by removing exactly one thing at a time, 256 calls, 400 nodes /
1600 edges, assigned-private storage:

  nx   dv[i]                      102.9 ns/call
  fnx  dv[i]   (2 Python frames)  155.9 ns/call
  fnx  same arithmetic, INLINE     57.3 ns/call   <- faster than networkx
  nx   dv(i)                      184.1 ns/call
  fnx  dv(i)                      232.5 ns/call

The arithmetic was never the deficit - inlined it BEATS networkx. The whole gap
was frame overhead at roughly 49ns a frame: __getitem__ delegated to a helper,
so a subscript cost two frames where networkx's costs one.

The body is not duplicated. It moved into __getitem__; __call__'s scalar path
runs the membership test it already needed and delegates there, so the degree is
computed in one place and the helper is gone.

